# (build 133) A window asked for while the screen scrolls. ProcessWindows
# (ps2.asm:13502) tests the main camera's x and y against the 16px grid
# before it starts a window, and off it returns (loc_9478) -- the word
# waits and is tried every frame, so the window opens as the step ends.
# In Aukba the step down from 12,12 scrolls the screen; A four pixels in,
# at nothing. Five ticks later the frame at 160,196 is still the map
# ($888): without the test the box is already opening there (index 11,
# $800), and slides with plane A for the rest of the step. Then $1708,
# "There seems to be nothing unusual here." Until build 133 the port never
# answered A mid-step, so the case did not arise.

start level 10 11 9          # Aukba
wait screen level
wait idle
press right                  # 12,9
wait idle
walk down 3                  # 12,12, on the camera's follow line
wait step
walk down 1                  # this step scrolls the screen
wait ticks 2
press a                      # four pixels in, nothing ahead
wait ticks 5
expect pixel 160 196 $888    # the map: no window yet
shot 01_mid_scroll
wait step
expect level 10 12 13
wait idle
expect script $1708
shot 02_opened
